{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And it became a serpent.</b> The first of the signs that he performed for Pharaoh was the תנין, and it is a serpent (נחש); thus the Holy One, blessed be He, said to him in the plague of blood: ״והמטה אשר נהפך לנחש״. And the reason that it turned into a serpent and not into other beasts and animals such as a horse or an ox, a lion or a wolf, is this: because the serpent sinned and caused Chavah to sin with the tongue, and likewise Pharaoh the wicked sinned with the tongue — he it who said (Exodus 5:2): ״מי ה׳ אשר אשמע בקולו לא ידעתי את ה׳״ — and because of this the first of the signs was a serpent, to hint to him that he would be punished for his sin just as the serpent was punished. And we find that all who hurl words heavenward are punished with the bite of the serpent, as it is written (Numbers 21:6): ״וידבר העם באלהים ובמשה״, and it is written (ibid.): ״וישלח ה׳ בעם את הנחשים השרפים וינשכו את העם״. Furthermore, just as the serpent twists and extends and does not remain in one state, so Pharaoh the wicked hardened his heart and grew firm in his wickedness, and with the weight of the plagues he would agree to send Israel forth, and afterward he turned again and hardened his heart — as it is written (Exodus 8:11): ״וירא פרעה כי היתה הרוחה והכבד את לבו״. And the reason Scripture expressed it in the term תנין is because Pharaoh is called a תנין, as it is said (Ezekiel 29:3): ״התנים הגדול הרובץ בתוך יאוריו״, and it hinted to him thereby that just as Aharon's staff swallowed their staffs, so the Holy One, blessed be He, is destined to swallow Pharaoh and his army in the Sea of Reeds." "<b>By way of the Midrash.</b> ״ויהיו לתנינים״ — Pharaoh said: Such is the nature of your Elohim — sorceries come forth from here into the world."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:56:45.458089605Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}